    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Heart failure with preserved ejection fraction, improving (I50.32)</content>. Echocardiography confirms preserved ejection fraction (62 percent) with an enlarged left atrium and raised filling pressures. She is still mildly congested, and kidney function and potassium are stable on the new medicines (eGFR 58, potassium 3.9). [S]<list><item>Continue furosemide 20 mg daily and empagliflozin 10 mg daily.</item><item>Start spironolactone 12.5 mg daily, since blood pressure is above target and potassium and kidney function are stable.</item><item>Repeat the basic metabolic panel in one to two weeks after starting spironolactone, by the CMID schedule.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertensive heart disease (I11.0)</content>. Blood pressure 146/80 mmHg, above the 130/80 target. [S]<list><item>Spironolactone is expected to lower it; recheck at the three-month review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel with magnesium</td><td>1 to 2 weeks after starting or changing therapy; every 3 to 6 months when stable</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two weeks after starting furosemide and empagliflozin. Sodium, potassium, creatinine, and magnesium normal; eGFR 58, a small expected fall</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Transthoracic echocardiogram</td><td>At diagnosis; repeat only with unexplained change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Ejection fraction 62 percent, left atrial volume index 42 mL/m², E/e&apos; 16: heart failure with preserved ejection fraction</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure, heart rate, weight, jugular venous pressure, edema, lungs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Weight down 1.7 kg; jugular venous pressure and edema improved</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>NYHA functional class</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Class II</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>KCCQ-12</td><td>Baseline, then every 3 to 6 months</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Baseline 52 at intake; next at the three-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Cardiology evaluation for specific causes</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today. Cardiac amyloidosis is not suspected: septal thickness 11 mm, voltage criteria for left ventricular hypertrophy on the ECG, and no carpal tunnel or neuropathy</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>SGLT2 inhibitor tolerance</td><td>Each visit while starting</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No volume depletion, genital infection, or urinary infection</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Daily weight diary</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed; she records every morning</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Reach euvolemia with no ankle edema and a stable dry weight within three months. In progress; target 1905-06-29 [S]</item><item>Improve the KCCQ-12 overall summary score by at least 15 points by the three-month review. In progress; target 1905-06-29 [S]</item><item>Lower blood pressure below 130/80 by the six-month review without orthostatic symptoms. In progress; target 1905-09-28 [S]</item><item>Resume a full speaking and travel schedule by the six-month review. In progress; target 1905-09-28 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Respiratory syncytial virus vaccine, single dose [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); 2023 ACC Expert Consensus Decision Pathway on Management of Heart Failure With Preserved Ejection Fraction (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, heart failure monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Basic metabolic panel in one to two weeks after starting spironolactone. Heart failure review in three months. Next scheduled visit 1905-06-29: three-month heart failure and blood pressure review. [S]</paragraph></text>

